{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"Updated [migration.sql](<RUNNER_ROOT>/results/hb-devhard-043-gpt54-medium-host4-r1/trials/002-codex-attempt-001/hb-work/codex/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260821-132422-4f2a2f1a/workspace/in/db/migration.sql) to do a transactional SQLite table rebuild that preserves all users, preserves `orders.user_id` references, keeps `created_at`, applies the required deterministic email cleanup for `u4`/`u5`/`u6`, adds `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`, and stays rerunnable. It also keeps `users_pre_migration_backup` for rollback and `users_status_backup` plus triggers so reruns preserve later status changes.\n\nCreated [preflight_report.md](<RUNNER_ROOT>/results/hb-devhard-043-gpt54-medium-host4-r1/trials/002-codex-attempt-001/hb-work/codex/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260821-132422-4f2a2f1a/workspace/in/db/preflight_report.md), [rollback.sql](<RUNNER_ROOT>/results/hb-devhard-043-gpt54-medium-host4-r1/trials/002-codex-attempt-001/hb-work/codex/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260821-132422-4f2a2f1a/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql), [postcheck.sql](<RUNNER_ROOT>/results/hb-devhard-043-gpt54-medium-host4-r1/trials/002-codex-attempt-001/hb-work/codex/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260821-132422-4f2a2f1a/workspace/in/db/postcheck.sql), and [migration_report.md](<RUNNER_ROOT>/results/hb-devhard-043-gpt54-medium-host4-r1/trials/002-codex-attempt-001/hb-work/codex/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-043-db-migration-safety-gpt-5.4-20260821-132422-4f2a2f1a/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md). The rollback restores the original four-column `users` shape and original dirty email values from the backup snapshot.\n\nCommands run:\n```sh\nsed -n '1,240p' in/db/migration_policy.md\nsed -n '1,240p' in/db/schema.sql\nsed -n '1,240p' in/db/migration.sql\nsqlite3 --version\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" \"create table t(a int); alter table t add column if not exists b text; pragma table_info(t);\"\ncat <<'SQL' | sqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" ...   # sqlite shell .if probe\ncat <<'SQL' | sqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" ...   # transaction-on-error probe\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" < in/db/schema.sql\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" < in/db/migration.sql\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" < in/db/postcheck.sql\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" \"update users set status = 'disabled' where id = 'u4';\"\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" < in/db/migration.sql\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" \"select id, status from users where id = 'u4';\"\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" < in/db/rollback.sql\nsqlite3 \"$tmpdb\" \"select id, email is null as email_is_null, email = '' as email_is_blank from users where id in ('u5','u6') order by id;\"\ngit status --short\ngit rev-parse HEAD\ngit diff -- in/db/migration.sql in/db/preflight_report.md in/db/rollback.sql in/db/postcheck.sql in/db/migration_report.md\n```\n\nResults:\n- `postcheck.sql` passed on the migrated seed data.\n- A rerun preserved a changed `u4.status = 'disabled'`.\n- Rollback restored `u5.email` to `NULL` and `u6.email` to `''`, while keeping order rows.\n\nHead SHA: `e8c5272a251a9309192401e5a0acb9de1c543476`\n\nAssumption/risk:\n- The migration assumes the dirty legacy email cases are the documented rows `u4`, `u5`, and `u6`. Additional unexpected duplicate emails outside that set would still fail the new unique constraint rather than being auto-remediated."}}
